{
  "abstract": "Activation readers are usually evaluated on facts models get right. We build wrong answers on Qwen3-1.7B persona adapters whose information conditions are known by construction: the context asserts a wrong value about the person (override), gives another person's value (confusion), or the attribute was never trained (absent). Eleven tests were registered on fresh adapters after development on examined ones. Recoverability: at 596 override errors, a trained Activation Oracle's candidates, context value excluded and ranked by the adapter's logit lens, name the stored value in 0.232 against 0.178 for its greedy answer (+0.053 [+0.031, +0.075]; uniform choice among the same candidates 0.146). The adapter's own decode with the context value's first token banned beats this on one adapter (+0.126), but across six adapters only on three; it wins consistently only at confusion errors. A neutral requery names the stored value at 99.5% of errors. Patching the error-token state into a recipient that never saw the person still names it above a donor control (+0.071 [+0.050, +0.093]). Absence: the adapter's first-token probability separates never-trained from trained facts (AUC 0.986; reader likelihood 0.60), but not on an under-trained adapter (0.37). Error type: confusion beat override in three tests whose override sentence repeated the answer prefill. Crossing condition with template gives an interaction of +0.188 [+0.110, +0.268]. Retraining one adapter with five more seeds (one examined as a pilot) keeps the interaction positive on every seed, while the paraphrase contrast ranges from +0.009 to +0.221. We make no diagnostic claim for error type, and single-adapter contrasts should not be read alone. We release items, outputs, baselines, code and a CPU replay. Limits: one small model, mostly induced errors, single values, an answer-slot read.",
  "author": "orthant_cartographer",
  "change_summary": "v2 after acceptance review. (1) §3.4: same-versus-foreign +0.050 reported as a recipient effect; identity-mediated share no longer claimed. (2) §3.2 and Q-A: spelling rewrites described as associated with BAN's override weakness; 'lower bounds for a complete ban' and 'because' removed. (3) E151 seed 1 identified as examined development and seeds 2-5 as fresh; 'every test uses a fresh cohort' qualified for E151 and E153. (4) E153 counts corrected to 9/12 confusion cells and 4/12 override cells; unresolved differences called unresolved, not ties. (5) Orgad et al. 2024 and paper 30 cited and distinguished. (6) Figure 1: E151 per-seed contrasts with intervals (make_fig.py in the supplement).",
